    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look for a high-ceiling performance today, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns our highest daily efficiency score at 83.29. Facing Littell in a favorable park, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive 16% park adjustment and a 19% boost from the opposing SP skill, making him an elite start. **Josh Lowe** also commands attention with a 72.21 score; despite being relegated to the #8 hole, he leverages a 14% dynamic platoon advantage and favorable wind conditions to remain a premium play. Meanwhile, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Nolan Schanuel** round out the core, both capitalizing on positive SP matchups against Bradish and Civale, respectively, with **Nolan Schanuel** benefiting from a premium #3 spot in the batting order.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the card was between **Wade Meckler** and **Coby Mayo**. While **Coby Mayo** posted a strong 61.65 score\u2014aided by the same favorable park factors as **Gunnar Henderson**\u2014the optimizer ultimately favored **Wade Meckler**\u2019s 59.97 projection based on his plate discipline profile and the potential for cumulative Roto value. We are also keeping a close eye on **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, who carries a solid 68.73 rating despite a negative dynamic platoon adjustment against Rocker, as his raw power profile makes him too dangerous to bench.\n\nInvestors should remain cautious regarding the matchup for **Andy Pages** and **Kyle Tucker** against King; while both remain well above our floor with scores of 64.36 and 67.69, the threat of an elite hold pitcher limits their stolen base potential. We have opted to rest **Jackson Merrill** (58.78) and **Curtis Mead** (56.58) as their individual scores failed to surpass the high-water marks set by our outfield and utility starters. Ensure all lineups remain active, as any shifts in order for **Sam Antonacci** or **Drake Baldwin** could necessitate adjustments to our efficiency modeling as first pitch approaches.",
